#!/bin/sh
# ExecStart wrapper for pidp11-simh.service. systemd must not name
# /usr/bin/screen directly in ExecStart, for two independent reasons:
#
#   SELinux: the binary is screen_exec_t, and policy grants the transition into
#   screen_t to the legacy daemon domain only. systemd itself (init_t) is
#   denied { execute } and the unit dies at status=203/EXEC with
#   "Failed at step EXEC spawning /usr/bin/screen: Permission denied".
#   Executing it from a bin_t script starts screen from the unconfined service
#   domain, which is permitted.
#
#   screen's setgid bit (root:screen, which is what lets it create its socket
#   in /run/screen at 0775 root:screen) never takes effect under this unit:
#   AmbientCapabilities= makes systemd set NO_NEW_PRIVS, and that suppresses
#   setuid/setgid bits on exec. The unit compensates with
#   SupplementaryGroups=screen, so the group rather than the bit is what makes
#   the socket directory writable for the pidp11 user.
#
# Deliberately no SCREENDIR: keeping the compiled-in socket directory means
# pidp11-stop, and the sudoed "screen -ls/-x pidp11" that pdp11 runs for an
# operator, keep finding the session without extra environment in three places
# (sudo strips env by default, so SCREENDIR would have needed a sudoers Setenv
# as well to keep pdp11 working).
exec /usr/bin/screen "$@"
